Package: lsec
Version: __VERSION__
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: UnmetDecade <83873031+UnmetDecade@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: __INSTALLED_SIZE__
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), adduser
Recommends: clamav, clamav-daemon, clamav-freshclam, yara, lynis
Suggests: wazuh-agent
Description: Linux unified security client (daemon + web UI + CLI)
 lsec is a single-host security client that unifies read-only host auditing,
 on-demand ClamAV and YARA scanning, signed YARA rule-pack management,
 optional Falco alert ingestion and optional local Wazuh Agent alert
 ingestion behind one Web UI and HTTP API.
 .
 The package installs a hardened systemd unit. It never enables ClamAV
 on-access protection, never contacts a Wazuh Manager and never performs
 automatic file deletion or container changes. Container monitoring requires
 the separate read-only Docker proxy and is disabled by default.
